==Minigame==
{{sign|bwbuilding|Village Bridge Restaurant|Village Sandwiches are our specialty!}}
Under the [[Village Bridge]] there is a small sandwich van called the '''Village Bridge Restaurant''', which is noted for its specialty [[Berry]] sandwiches. This is the location of Baker Chris, whose battle details are shown above. In {{v2|Black and White|s}}, once defeated, Baker Chris will ask the player to temporarily help out, triggering a minigame. The object is to remember the orders of the four customers, repeat them to Chris, and then serve them in the correct order. The player will receive a [[Lum Berry]] as a reward. This can be done once per day.

In {{2v2|Black|White|2}}, the sandwich shop has been moved into one of the buildings; however, the minigame can no longer be played at it.

==In the manga==
===Pokémon Adventures===
Baker Chris makes her first appearance in ''[[PS486|Unraveling Mysteries]]'', where she meets up with {{adv|Black}} and {{adv|White}}. She takes them to the recently created [[Battle Subway]] after overhearing that Black wanted to know why [[Marshal]] had come to [[Nimbasa City]]. When White decides to become a Trainer, Chris lends her some Poké Balls so that she can capture a wild {{p|Deerling}}.

Chris later appears at the {{un|Pokémon League}} alongside several other Trainers to help battle Team Plasma.

